From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:31:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 33/47] hjviewer: same-account login: the account screens

What the app shows of the account in an account build (design v3 1-1 to 1-3,
1-7, 6-2 D1-D10), in two new files: hjviewer_account.dart with the hooks, the
dialogs and the requests, and hjviewer_account_texts.dart with every text in
Korean and English and the choices between them, plain Dart so that ci.sh tests
them with the bridge's web stand-in. src/lang stays as it is and no text holds
braces. The texts follow the app's language: Korean when translate() gives the
app's Korean words. One-line hooks in the shared files:

- login.dart: the first field is the Yonsei portal ID (D1). Once the login
  dialog closed with a login (D2), the first login takes the app to the
  accessible devices tab, and on Windows the PC tells what the login did with
  it: GET /api/hjv/this-device, then up to ten seconds for the service's
  hjv-pwless-state to turn active or disabled. "This PC is now in your device
  list" with [Remove this PC] (this-device/undo) when this login added it, the
  administrator's pause, "turns on shortly", another account's PC, a run
  without installing, or the server not confirming the PC; and, without a
  permanent password, the hint with [Set it now], which opens the security
  settings' password dialog behind the same administrator check (or unlock
  PIN) as those settings. The logout dialog of a PC this user's login bound
  says that logging out takes it out of the list (D3).
- peer_card.dart: "Add to address book" needs the address book (D4); the
  accessible devices' cards get "Remove from my list" and its confirmation,
  DELETE /api/hjv/devices/{id} (D5).
- toolbar.dart, the two settings pages: no session notes, which hjv-api does
  not keep (D6).
- desktop settings, Account (D7): this PC's line from the service's state, the
  PC password's line (permanent-password-set) with [Set], and the logged-in
  devices. The line names the owner (this-device: mine, another account's) and
  every state: on with the account's device count and [Turn off] (asked first,
  then hjv-pwless-off; anyone at the PC may), switched off here with [Turn on
  again] (the login dialog: only a login of the PC's account turns it on),
  paused, not in step with the server since the last list, a changed key,
  removed elsewhere with [Add again] (log out, then the login dialog), and a
  bind the server did not confirm.
- mobile settings, Account (D8): the logged-in devices.
- my_group.dart (D9): while hjv-api fails the kept cards stay, under a banner
  with [Retry]: the server's own text when it gave one (a clock ten minutes
  off), a locked iPhone's key, or "the HJViewer server cannot be used right
  now; password-less connections go on for a day". An empty list, once it
  came, says how a PC gets there.
- main.dart (D10): coming back to the front, at most every 30 seconds, the
  device list comes again quietly (currentUser first after a failure), and the
  account's devices nobody answered yet get the notice (GET /api/hjv/keys,
  "new": every key but this device's, whatever order the keys were made in,
  also one whose login ended since, until a device answers it; design v3
  U1-a, U1-c), with the login's time and network and what the device said of
  itself, [It is mine] (ack) or [Not me] (POST not-mine: logs the key out, or
  marks one that ended already). The title says whether the device logged in
  after this one, before it, or ended; an ended one's text says how and when,
  with its last password-less connection. A login dropped for want of its
  account key (hjv-relogin) is told, with [Log in], until the notice was closed
  once.

The logged-in devices: a row per device (the server's name and, but for an
iPhone's model code, the device's own in parentheses; login time, campus or
not, version, the last password-less connection) with [Log out]; opened, a
line per PC with its last use and 30-day count (U6); [Log out all other
devices]. A key already gone is said so. Below, the devices whose login ended
in the last 30 days, with how and when: logged out by itself, from which
device, expired, replaced by a new login of the device, past the account's 20
devices, by the administrator (U1-b). The questions before a logout from
another device and the dialog after it say what it does: no new password-less
connection, but a connection already open is not cut; it ends in the PC's
connection window, by "Restart remote device" from one's own device with the
PC's password, or with a restart of the PC (U1-d). Account requests go through
Rust's http_request, which signs them; a 401 ends the login as the device
list's does, but only for the token the app still keeps: a login sets the user
name before it stores its token, and the request the account settings send for
the new name can go out in that gap, with no token or the last login's.

The service's state as these screens read it (pc.rs, two strings): a bind
request whose binding the PC could not keep is refused as bind-store, like
the other bind refusals ("not confirmed by the server", [Add again]), not
as a bound PC's failed sync ([Turn off]) or "turns on shortly"; and an expired
list carries the time the last list came (expired <time>), so that the line
reads "not in step with the server (last checked 10/20 14:03)" (design 1-2).

Outside an account build every hook returns at once or leaves its condition
as it was; D4's address book condition holds for any build that turns the
address book off.

Tests: test/hjviewer_account_test.dart (pure, ci.sh): every service state to
its line and button for each owner, the after-login results to their notices,
the logout text, the logged-in devices' rows and opened lines from hjv-api's
answer and the ended ones with how they left, which keys get the new-device
notice (also older and ended ones), its titles and texts, the texts of a
logout that cuts no open connection, the banner, the empty list hint only once
the list came, the menu condition, the refresh interval, a 401 that ends the
login only for the token still kept, no braces.
test/hjviewer_account_widgets_test.dart (needs the generated bridge): the
logged-in devices list opening and logging out, the ended devices without
[Log out], this PC's lines with [Turn on again] only when switched off here,
the after-login notice's buttons, the new-device notice's answers, the notice
of a device that ended. src/hjviewer_account/pc/tests.rs: a bind whose
list cannot be kept is refused as bind-store, and the expired state has the
time of the last list.

Known limits: the desktop login's two-factor step, off with hjv-api (U1),
closes the login dialog as cancelled, so it gets no after-login screens. The
"removed elsewhere" line has no date: the service's state carries none. On
the account's only PC the accessible devices tab keeps the empty list hint:
hjv-api's device list leaves out the device that asks.

(Design v3, work package F: patch 0033.)

